        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "e36514e5-7403-3c4b-8b36-daf45599916f",
                "word": "adversité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0522f1cd-0180-4962-9d11-485594e94f59",
                        "entry_id": "e36514e5-7403-3c4b-8b36-daf45599916f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "adversités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                        "entry_id": "e36514e5-7403-3c4b-8b36-daf45599916f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "État, situation de celui qui éprouve les rigueurs du sort."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abfc87cc-3da7-44e7-b14f-9dc80466feb2",
                                "sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                                "text": "Être dans l’adversité. — Tomber dans l’adversité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92f99426-e6c1-4cd2-ae73-e5d030069049",
                                "sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                                "text": "Être constant dans l’adversité. — Succomber à l’adversité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3cce2e1a-8415-4564-ab5c-fb2ba3a80525",
                                "sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                                "text": "Il fallait réfléchir à la tactique que nous devrions adopter pour ne point succomber devant l'adversité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77bb3e0a-aa89-4ff7-8dac-70a15c5ddad1",
                                "sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                                "text": "Il a dû faire un pacte avec l’adversité car il paraît s’y mouvoir avec de captivantes immunités, oui, il a des accointances avec le mauvais sort."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "43b3182d-faa5-4bbb-9a60-55383e0dadf8",
                                "sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                                "text": "Le fils d’anciens collabos qui avaient su échapper à l’épuration avait appris de ses parents l’expression « Sale Juif ! » et il la répétait à loisir ! Je devais avoir sept ans, je m’en souviens encore et je me dis qu’après tout une certaine dose d’adversité peut être un bon moteur dans la vie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "37c719f9-697b-4b5e-974c-b988cce17113",
                        "source_entry_id": "e36514e5-7403-3c4b-8b36-daf45599916f",
                        "source_sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                        "target_lang_word": "Widrigkeit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Widrigkeit",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c934055a-5459-3f8d-a24f-c449bae7d3ca",
                                        "entry_id": "f4a6d997-81d1-3851-8010-35163562f277",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "etwas, das sich als Hemmnis erweist"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32ac119d-e25b-4a59-9065-b6cc751d57a2",
                                                "sense_id": "c934055a-5459-3f8d-a24f-c449bae7d3ca",
                                                "text": "„Auf seinen zwei vorangegangenen Reisen hatte sich Cook derlei Widrigkeiten in der Regel mit Gleichmut gestellt und im Umgang mit Matrosen und Einheimischen eine strenge, aber gerechte Hand bewiesen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f7080b7-d25d-4547-b8ff-903c5f1bd0a5",
                                                "sense_id": "c934055a-5459-3f8d-a24f-c449bae7d3ca",
                                                "text": "„Der erneute Drehstopp ist nicht die einzige Widrigkeit für die Sexfilmer: Neben der Kostenlos-Kultur im Internet bedroht auch noch eine Neuregelung im Bezirk Los Angeles ihr Geschäftsmodell. Dort sind Pornodarsteller nun gesetzlich verpflichtet, sich beim Dreh mit Kondomen zu schützen.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c3f62369-4f7b-4f88-829b-eca24dd0c092",
                        "source_entry_id": "e36514e5-7403-3c4b-8b36-daf45599916f",
                        "source_sense_id": "fb9c50bf-211b-32c2-80ea-16bb981f47a7",
                        "target_lang_word": "adversity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "adversity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1b30c85-8cf0-3f35-9be0-7c210397f9d5",
                                        "entry_id": "b82e8b52-4055-3811-a2b4-805e20caf59b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of adverse conditions; state of misfortune or calamity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd605000-3666-4501-bb9a-27c189c35a7e",
                                                "sense_id": "f1b30c85-8cf0-3f35-9be0-7c210397f9d5",
                                                "text": "The doctor loved the squire, loved him as his oldest friend; but he loved him ten times better as being in adversity than he could ever have done had things gone well at Greshansbury in his time."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1204c5f4-2715-4993-b77e-8df4f7a52482",
                                                "sense_id": "f1b30c85-8cf0-3f35-9be0-7c210397f9d5",
                                                "text": "God approves all adversity. Not all adversity that the Christian encounters is due to sins in the Christian's life. Not all adversity is the fault of the Christian."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fafbb649-dc47-46ed-a693-b2d5505897ba",
                                                "sense_id": "f1b30c85-8cf0-3f35-9be0-7c210397f9d5",
                                                "text": "These are the people who will overcome the adversity, chaos, and destruction of combat and defeat the enemy in war."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36bced25-9416-36af-86c9-317b80cb2894",
                                        "entry_id": "b82e8b52-4055-3811-a2b4-805e20caf59b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An event that is adverse; calamity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72f64d4d-756f-452a-80d6-fd4edf45e32e",
                                                "sense_id": "36bced25-9416-36af-86c9-317b80cb2894",
                                                "text": "Having “secret notice,” the writer of “True Remembrances” declares of the above complains, he retired into Munster, intending to proceed to England, to justify himself; but was detained there for want of money by the breaking out of rebellion. This adversity befell him in the autumn of 1598."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b84cf27-2b35-49d9-ad11-949b34e7ec98",
                                                "sense_id": "36bced25-9416-36af-86c9-317b80cb2894",
                                                "text": "Every family is struck by adversity at one time or another. No matter how mature the patients are, regardless of the care an advantages they give their children, despite a desirable interactive love between family members, adversity will attack any family"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ed212ee-fa4f-4918-94cd-f97895971d93",
                                                "sense_id": "36bced25-9416-36af-86c9-317b80cb2894",
                                                "text": "Make sure that your child’s adversity is really an adversity. Not having parents who can buy a new car upon your son’s sixteenth birthday is not an adversity. Being the only girl on the block who doesn’t own a designed handbag is not an adversity"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a29b14c4-effc-43ba-969f-612ddcd1bc0a",
                        "source_entry_id": "e36514e5-7403-3c4b-8b36-daf45599916f",
